# Trivy baseline for eg-esign — reviewed 2026-07-27.
#
# Only findings with no trivial fix belong here. Anything not listed still
# fails the build, so new vulnerabilities are caught.
#
# Fixed rather than ignored in the same change (16 -> 5): axios ^1.18.0,
# fast-uri ^3.1.4, brace-expansion ^5.0.8, @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger
# ^2.9.0, next 16.2.11, sharp ^0.35.0.
#
# Verified against the built image: react-router, sharp and brace-expansion do
# ship in the runtime image, so these are real exposures, not dev-tree noise.
# Re-triage when the nightly upstream-sync bumps these.

# react-router 7.18.1 -> 8.3.0. A 7->8 major of the app's own framework
# (apps/remix runs React Router in framework mode) — its own project, not a
# CI-unblocking patch.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# postcss 8.4.31 -> 8.5.12 / 8.5.18. Nested inside `next` as
# node_modules/next/node_modules/postcss; root postcss is already 8.5.19 and
# the existing overrides entry doesn't reach a workspace-nested copy.
CVE-2026-45623
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849

# brace-expansion 2.1.2 -> 5.0.8. Root is overridden to 5.0.8; @hono/vite-dev-server,
# filelist and google-gax keep a nested 2.x that npm overrides don't rewrite.
CVE-2026-14257

# sharp 0.34.5 -> 0.35.0. Attempted and reverted: 0.35.0 restructured its type
# declarations, so the pruned Docker build fails with TS7016 "Could not find a
# declaration file for module 'sharp'" in packages/lib/utils/images/*. Needs
# @types/sharp or upstream code changes, not a version bump.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
